#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""UseCert stack-5 cutover kit: the host-side commands that take the stack-5 vaults from
"deployed" to "live" (docs/STACK5-DEPLOY-RUNBOOK.md, "Cutover kit").

    usecert-s5-cutover <subcommand> [--dry-run] [--offline --workdir DIR] [options]

Each subcommand names the host it runs on and refuses to run anywhere else. Each is idempotent:
run again after success, it changes nothing; faced with state it does not expect, it refuses and
says what it saw. None of them prints, logs or copies a private key.

  MONTREAL  (user usecert; forge; the deployer key in /etc/usecert/mainnet-deployer.env)
    bootstrap        usecert-mainnet-bootstrap for the vaults not yet bootstrapped, then read back
                     bootstrapped() and lighterAccountIndex(); writes /opt/usecert-s5/accounts.json
    phase-a          pubkeys.env + venue minimums -> SafeBatches phaseA() (build only) -> a signing
                     page (EIP-712 SafeTx, one signature per owner and batch) in /opt/usecert-s5/phaseA
    phase-b          SafeBatches phaseB() (build only; refuses before the two-day notice)
    open             SafeBatches openMinting() for --vaults (uTSLA first) -> signing page
    exec-safe        owner signatures -> checkSignatures -> anvil fork -> execTransaction -> read-back
  FRANCE    (keeper host)
    genkeys          (as keeper) one venue API key per vault; pubkeys.env holds public halves only
    keeper-configs   (as root) /opt/keeper/vaults/s5-<sym>.json, book-stack5.json, systemd drop-ins
                     (installed, not started); --start once phase B is on chain
    signer-cutover   (as root) the signer on 8787 moves to the stack-5 book; --rollback undoes it
    funding-relay    (as root) unit + timer + stack-5 drop-in, one --dry-run pass; --enable
  WORKSTATION (the contracts checkout; the front-end branch is in the same repository)
    site-build       the front-end contract bundle from the stack-5 book, on frontend/total-return,
                     as an LF tar for usecert-deploy-web on France

--dry-run   every read and every check, no transaction, no systemctl, no file outside --workdir.
--offline   (implies --dry-run) no network and no host: the chain is simulated from the book and
            kept in <workdir>/sim-chain.json, so a sequence of offline runs follows the real one.
            Everything the simulator answers is labelled SIM. It proves the plumbing, not the chain.
"""
